<p align="left" class="body1"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-21 | Tuesday</font></strong><br/><br/>And here we are sitting through another Tuesday.<br>
<br>
Tomorrow night is the big night.  By the time you read this, the <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> show at the Showbox, November 22nd, will be sold out, cuzzo.<br>
<br>
In other music related news, check out the new feature on the site!  In
the upper right corner of your browser, there's a flash image of a
graphic equalizer and a link directly beneath it.  This link is the
"free weekly mp3," or at least, it will be until we think of a more
cutting edge name for it.  The downloads will be anything from
unreleased MassLine material, to mixtape tracks, to maybe just good
Seattle music that we think you need to get hip to.<br>
<br>
We're currently featuring <strong>Blue Scholars - Inkwell (Crashed Cop Car Remix)</strong> since we're still getting a bunch of requests for it.<br>
<br>
If you have any particular interests as far as what music should be available
for download, then don't be a sukka and just think it!  Go post your ideas in the forum!<br>
<br>
Thas thas whassup.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-20 | Monday</font></strong><br/><br/><span style="display: inline"><p class="massline-embed-gap">Archived embedded media is unavailable for offline playback. <a class="massline-external-playback" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m3GstYOIc0I" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open video m3GstYOIc0I on YouTube (external playback)</a></p><br><br/></br></span><span class="body1 style73"><span style="display: inline">Iranian-American,
U.S. CITIZEN and UCLA student, Mostafa Tabatabainejad, was shot by
UCLA'S UCPD November 14th 2006, because he could not show his Student
ID. He was shot 5 times with a taser gun. Police threatened to shoot
students who got too close. The Student yelled out that he had a
medical condition, but the cops kept shooting. </span></span><span style="display: inline"><br><br>Somebody caught the whole ordeal on their camera phone.</br></br></span><span style="display: inline"> <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://dailybruin.com/news/articles.asp?id=38960" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>The Daily Bruin</strong></a> wrote an article about it, and <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://mideastyouth.com/?p=547" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>MideastYouth.com</strong></a> also has something about the incident.<br><br>Let us know what you think.<br><br><br>Saba<br/></br></br></br></br></br></span><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-19 | Sunday</font></strong><br/><br/>"<strong>Hip Hop: Back To It's Roots</strong>" was in Seattle this weekend, a play written &amp; directed by <strong>Melissa Noelle-Greene</strong> complete with workshops at the <strong>Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center</strong>... feauturing none other then <strong>Davey D </strong>of <strong><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://myspace.com/mrdaveyd" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hard-Knock Radio</a></strong>.  word is they had a press conference with <strong>Talib Kweli</strong> and <strong>survivors of Hurricane Katrina </strong>who are now living in the Northwest.  if anyone out there made it out to this event, let us know how it went in <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://masslinemedia.com/smf" rel="noopener noreferrer">the forums</a>.<br><br>On the subject of Hurricane Katrina, our sista <strong>Walidah Imarisha</strong> put together an amazing documentary on the subject called "<strong>Finding Common Ground in New Orleans</strong>" you can find more information on this subject off her <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://myspace.com/channelzeromedia" rel="noopener noreferrer">myspace site</a> and the film is being distributed by <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://twn.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Third World Newsreel</strong></a>.<br><br>I also wanted to give a shout-out to the homies <strong>Asun</strong> &amp; <strong>Jerm</strong> of <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://myspace.com/1stplatoon" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Alpha-P</strong></a> who are wrapping up a tour tonight in Las Vegas with <strong>Himself</strong>, and <strong>Sleep</strong> of Oldominion at the <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://myspace.com/sundayskoolin" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Sunday Skoolin'</strong></a>.<br><br>and on a more personal note, i finished a mix-tape last week entitled "<strong>Westlake: Class Of 1999</strong>"... 22 tracks recorded in 3 citys over the last 4 years that never had a home... juss a lil somethin' to hold you over till the national release of <strong>Lovework</strong> coming February '07.  you can get more details and order the mixtape off <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://myspace.com/gabrielteodros" rel="noopener noreferrer">myspace.com/gabrielteodros</a><br><br>Now go catch Talib Kweli and Buckshot at the Showbox, tonight at 8pm.  let us know how it goes.......<br><br>-- gt<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-18 | Saturday</font></strong><br/><br/>four thumbs down for 4pm sunsets.  the inhabitants of the northwest are patiently waiting for the sun to return so we can live normal lives again that don't involve crippling depression...<br><br>but on a lighter note!  <br><br>today is ultimate sportsfan day. if i wasn't havin dinner with my mom, i'd probably be in the soufend watching the pacquiao/morales fight.  one of the most anticipated matchups of the year.<br><br>grab a san pelligrino, some hummus, and embrace the animalistic side of your human nature by watching two men beat each other senseless.<br><br/><br/>howla.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-16 | Thursday</font></strong><br/><br/>for all thugs with a heart, <strong>Lyfe Jennings</strong> is performing tonight at the Showbox.  assuming i can get all my work done for the day, i'll be there for shure.<br><br>speaking of things that are filthy, check it out...<br><br>the new Artist Handstyle Tee is HERE!<br/><br/><img align="middle" alt="" height="241" src="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/assets/374cd34977dd7831096b.jpg" width="430"><br/><br/>this month's shirt is brought to you by <strong>peekaboo!</strong><br/>from Seattle, WA and the Islamic Republic of Iran. you may have seen<br/>peekaboo!'s art at shows, on shoes, skateboards around the town...<br/>shooooot, you've likely seen something of his somewhere! i mean, the<br/>young man's been playing with himself since 1983.<br/><br/>he reps a crew called <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://myspace.com/pocketfullofmonsters" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pocket Full Of Monsters</a>.<br/>if you like their work--which we certainly do--you're in luck because<br/>peeks is just the first of this camp to represent on MassLine cloth. <br/><br/>these items will be available <strong>FIRST</strong> at the <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> show, <strong>November 22nd</strong> at the <strong>Showbox</strong>.<br/><br/>speaking of the ThingsTaken show, one of the opening acts, OneSelf, was written about in the Stranger.  check 'em out <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005912/http://thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=104379" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.<br/><br/>til next time,<br/><br/>saba<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><center><div class="pagenumbers"><a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a8bd5dc9e78f.php">[&lt;&lt;]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-ff41e4b899bf.php">[1]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f09e4ab70de0.php">[2]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-13fd6b501db4.php">[3]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a6d8d32ad781.php">[4]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-d45f54b0cbc4.php">[5]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-0bfc403792bc.php">[6]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-fd78b8847920.php">[7]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-cd30dd4ecbb4.php">[8]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3f0473af164e.php">[9]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-328a9b624d92.php">[10]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3c1fe8996261.php">[11]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-86e16e039033.php">[12]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-7e9b30d94f52.php">[13]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a4c814fd9062.php">[14]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-9413aa1ebf0f.php">[15]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-c3d2d6995e50.php">[16]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-9d70a3c73aca.php">[17]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f6fd84ec4403.php">[18]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-aeb25bb8527b.php">[19]</a